# Sources of the natural-language lane study (hub 3.10). Old-body files were read at head b8ff978c9 unless a node names an earlier revision; 'rev' is the last commit that touched the file. Line ranges sit in the citing claim.

n: 2.18
name: natural-language-lane-sources
kind: hub
is: The primary sources behind hub 3.10: the study report on the old body's natural-language lane, the translator with its lexicon, projector, coverage lens and band, the grammar engine and text normaliser under it, two files read at the revision before the cut of 2026-09-29, the word, code, phrase and wordnet tables beside the translator, the dictionary of numeric meaning recipes with its crossing cell, the first-round critique, and two files the review of the hub added: a sample grammar for arithmetic sentences and the one band that calls the dictionary's names.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 2.18.1
name: gap-natural-language-lane.md
kind: source
is: The study report on the old body's natural-language lane, 584 lines: what the translator does, which claims a standing test covers, the neighbouring tables, seven separate neutral-id schemes, and what to carry forward or drop. The study ran no Form or BML program; every verdict number in the report is a number recorded in a file.
path: coherence-seed/study/r2/gap-natural-language-lane.md
